From e98eb5fa203c3c5d26b8c141e3e712d7ddf98d71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
by: triplecN
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] shunko: exclude runtime addnode targets while they are
 disconnected

Patch 0019 promised that the automatic Shunko path skips nodes added with the
addnode RPC whether or not they are connected. That did not hold while such a
node was down: CConnman::GetAddedNodeInfo only fills resolvedAddress for
currently connected peers, so the code pushed a default (invalid) address into
the exclusion list and the real address stayed selectable.

Remember the configured string as well (Lookup without DNS, as for -connect),
and skip an invalid resolvedAddress. Startup -connect/-addnode/-seednode
behavior is unchanged.

Regression: tests/shunko_regtest.py [6b] now also restarts the node without
-connect, adds the dead onion with the addnode RPC, and asserts the automatic
path still reports "No known nodes" while the explicit path accepts it.
---
 src/rpc/mempool.cpp | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/rpc/mempool.cpp b/src/rpc/mempool.cpp
index ea61b3a..c9a07a9 100644
--- a/src/rpc/mempool.cpp
+++ b/src/rpc/mempool.cpp
@@ -288,7 +288,16 @@ static RPCHelpMan shunkobroadcast()
                 for (const std::string& s : gArgs.GetArgs("-seednode")) remember_configured(s);
                 if (node.connman) {
                     for (const AddedNodeInfo& info : node.connman->GetAddedNodeInfo(/*include_connected=*/true)) {
-                        configured.push_back(static_cast<const CNetAddr&>(info.resolvedAddress));
+                        // A disconnected added node has no resolved address:
+                        // GetAddedNodeInfo only fills resolvedAddress for peers
+                        // that are currently connected. Remember the configured
+                        // string as well, so a node added at runtime with the
+                        // addnode RPC is excluded while it is down too. The
+                        // string resolves without DNS for IPs and .onion names.
+                        if (info.resolvedAddress.IsValid()) {
+                            configured.push_back(static_cast<const CNetAddr&>(info.resolvedAddress));
+                        }
+                        remember_configured(info.m_params.m_added_node);
                     }
                 }
                 const auto is_configured = [&](const CService& s) {
